e cut with a saw, never with shears.","token_count":22},{"alternates":[],"best_rank_by_intent":{"I1":2},"char_end":656,"char_start":564,"chunk_id":"Doc_07§2.1#1","citation":"Doc_07 §2.1","conflict_ids":[],"document_id":"Doc_07","evidence_id":"Doc_07§2.1#1","fused_score":0.032002,"hits":[{"bm25_rank":2,"dense_rank":3,"intent_id":"I1","query_id":"Q1","rank":2,"rerank_score":null,"retrieval_method":"hybrid_rrf","rrf_score":0.03200204813108039,"score":0.03200204813108039,"stale":false}],"intent_relevance":{},"label":"E2","section_id":"2.1","section_title":"Ladder Safety","selected_for":["I1"],"source_path":"Doc_07_fixture_orchard.txt","supporting_intents":["I1"],"supporting_queries":["Q1"],"text":"Ladders are permitted in the orchard only when a second worker holds the base of the ladder.","token_count":17},{"alternates":[],"best_rank_by_intent":{"I1":3},"char_end":767,"char_start":678,"chunk_id":"Doc_07§2.2#1","citation":"Doc_07 §2.2","conflict_ids":[],"document_id":"Doc_07","evidence_id":"Doc_07§2.2#1","fused_score":0.031498,"hits":[{"bm25_rank":3,"dense_rank":4,"intent_id":"I1","query_id":"Q1","rank":3,"rerank_score":null,"retrieval_method":"hybrid_rrf","rrf_score":0.03149801587301587,"score":0.03149801587301587,"stale":false}],"intent_relevance":{},"label":"E3","section_id":"2.2","section_title":"Ladder Storage","selected_for":["I1"],"source_path":"Doc_07_fixture_orchard.txt","supporting_intents":["I1"],"supporting_queries":["Q1"],"text":"Ladders are not permitted in the orchard overnight and must be returned to the tool shed.","token_count":16},{"alternates":[],"best_rank_by_intent":{"I1":4,"I2":5},"char_end":1398,"char_start":1276,"chunk_id":"Doc_07§4#1","citation":"Doc_07 §4","conflict_ids":[],"document_id":"Doc_07","evidence_id":"Doc_07§4#1","fused_score":0.016129,"hits":[{"bm25_rank":null,"dense_rank":2,"intent_id":"I1","query_id":"Q1","rank":4,"rerank_score":null,"retrieval_method":"hybrid_rrf","rrf_score":0.016129032258064516,"score":0.016129032258064516,"stale":false},{"bm25_rank":null,"dense_rank":5,"intent_id":"I2","query_id":"Q2","rank":5,"rerank_score":null,"retrieval_method":"hybrid_rrf","rrf_score":0.015384615384615385,"score":0.015384615384615385,"stale":false}],"intent_relevance":{},"label":"E4","section_id":"4","section_title":"Tool Shed","selected_for":["I1"],"source_path":"Doc_07_fixture_orchard.txt","supporting_intents":["I1","I2"],"supporting_queries":["Q1","Q2"],"text":"Before leaving the shed, each worker must:\n1. Clean the blades.\n2. Hang every tool on its hook.\n3. Sign the tool register.","token_count":23},{"alternates":[],"best_rank_by_intent":{"I2":2},"char_end":454,"char_start":313,"chunk_id":"fixture_lighthouse_manual§1.1#1","citation":"fixture_lighthouse_manual §1.1","conflict_ids":[],"document_id":"fixture_lighthouse_manual","evidence_id":"fixture_lighthouse_manual§1.1#1","fused_score":0.016129,"hits":[{"bm25_rank":null,"dense_rank":2,"intent_id":"I2","query_id":"Q2","rank":2,"rerank_score":null,"retrieval_method":"hybrid_rrf","rrf_score":0.016129032258064516,"score":0.016129032258064516,"stale":false}],"intent_relevance":{},"label":"E5","section_id":"1.1","section_title":"Wick Trimming","selected_for":["I2"],"source_path":"fixture_lighthouse_manual.md","supporting_intents":["I2"],"supporting_queries":["Q2"],"text":"Wicks are trimmed to a height of 4 millimetres. A wick trimmed too short produces a dim beam; a wick left too long produces soot on the lens.","token_count":28},{"alternates":[],"best_rank_by_intent":{"I2":3},"char_end":1260,"char_start":789,"chunk_id":"Doc_07§3#1","citation":"Doc_07 §3","conflict_ids":[],"document_id":"Doc_07","evidence_id":"Doc_07§3#1","fused_score":0.015873,"hits":[{"bm25_rank":null,"dense_rank":3,"intent_id":"I2","query_id":"Q2","rank":3,"rerank_score":null,"retrieval_method":"hybrid_rrf","rrf_score":0.015873015873015872,"score":0.015873015873015872,"stale":false}],"intent_relevance":{},"label":"E6","section_id":"3","section_title":"Harvest Limits","selected_for":["I2"],"source_path":"Doc_07_fixture_orchard.txt","supporting_intents":["I2"],"supporting_queries":["Q2"],"text":"A picker may fill at most 40 crates per shift. Damaged fruit is placed in the compost bin, not in the crates. The harvest supervisor checks the crate count at the end of every shift. Crates are stacked no more than five high. Stacks taller than five crates must be split before the cart leaves the row. The cart driver confirms the stack height before moving. Fruit picked after sunset is recorded separately. Late fruit is stored in the cool room until the next morning.","token_count":85},{"alternates":[],"best_rank_by_intent":{"I1":5,"I2":4},"char_end":409,"char_start":145,"chunk_id":"Doc_07§1#1","citation":"Doc_07 §1","conflict_ids":[],"document_id":"Doc_07","evidence_id":"Doc_07§1#1","fused_score":0.015625,"hits":[{"bm25_rank":null,"dense_rank":5,"intent_id":"I1","query_id":"Q1","rank":5,"rerank_score":null,"retrieval_method":"hybrid_rrf","rrf_score":0.015384615384615385,"score":0.015384615384615385,"stale":false},{"bm25_rank":null,"dense_rank":4,"intent_id":"I2","query_id":"Q2","rank":4,"rerank_score":null,"retrieval_method":"hybrid_rrf","rrf_score":0.015625,"score":0.015625,"stale":false}],"intent_relevance":{},"label":"E7","section_id":"1","section_title":"Planting Schedule","selected_for":["I2"],"source_path":"Doc_07_fixture_orchard.txt","supporting_intents":["I1","I2"],"supporting_queries":["Q1","Q2"],"text":"Saplings in the fixture orchard are planted between the third and fifth week of the planting season. Each sapling receives 12 litres of water on the day it is planted.\n\nApproved sapling varieties:\n\n1. Red Fixture Apple\n\n2. Golden Fixture Pear\n\n3. Blue Fixture Plum","token_count":45}],"per_intent":[{"best_rank":1,"candidates":5,"covered":true,"evidence_ids":["Doc_07§2#1","Doc_07§2.1#1","Doc_07§2.2#1","Doc_07§4#1","Doc_07§1#1"],"intent_id":"I1","labels":["E1","E2","E3","E4","E7"],"query_id":"Q1","status":"ok"},{"best_rank":1,"candidate